      "type": "agent_message",
      "text": "I’ll verify the checked-out revision, then trace the limits and freshness rules across source, tests, and committed docs. I’ll use only the three registered local checks and won’t modify files."
    },
    {
      "type": "agent_message",
      "text": "The fixture exposes only the frozen verification interface, so I’m running all three allowed checks now. Their output should also establish the exact revision and clean working-tree boundary before I synthesize the source/test/docs evidence."
    },
    {
      "type": "agent_message",
      "text": "At commit `c9e8c2d`:\n\n- Canonical context: **1 MiB per file** (`1,048,576 bytes`).\n- Aggregate resume-read budget: **8 MiB** (`8,388,608 bytes`).\n- Always-loaded instruction budget: **32 KiB total** (`32,768 bytes`).\n\nSource, tests, and committed documentation agree on these boundaries. Exceeding either resource limit makes portable resume fail closed.\n\nStructural checkpoint validation is separate from freshness:\n\n- Structure requires every canonical section exactly once and in order, rejects unknown H2 sections, and ignores heading-like text inside fences, blockquotes, and CommonMark HTML blocks.\n- Passing that parser does **not** mean the checkpoint is current. Freshness is evaluated separately against Git state; a valid but stale checkpoint is reported as stale rather than treated as malformed.\n\nLocal checks actually run:\n\n- `format-check`: passed; 64 files checked.\n- `continuity-tests`: passed; 16/16 tests.\n- `git-diff`: exit 0; no changes."
    },
